Z||000008||RossT||07-25-2000||12:04 AM||||Pierre is close to me too.. I think I met Rob at the Dells Run.  He is the guy that is trying to collect every Fiero in SD. He gets calls from car dealers, Highway Patrol etc...<BR>telling him that they got another one for him!!!<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rob S||07-26-2000||10:40 AM||||Midwest Fieros Car Club is located in Onawa, Iowa, about 340 miles southeast of my home town of Pierre SD. It's about a five hour drive to club meetings! see web page (I haven't had time to update it since our show)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/midwestfieros/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/midwestfieros/</A> <P>I'm not trying to collect every Fiero in South Dakota, just those that need a home or are owned by someone who does not appreciate what they have! <BR>Rob Swanson<BR>Pierre SD<p>[This message has been edited by Rob S (edited 07-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||webbee||07-26-2000||03:22 PM||||There were about 75 people who said they would go to a mid country Pennock forum car show/get to gather a while back. At the moment that seems to be stalled. Since this is about mid country and is already happening next year, why don't we ALL make this a forum meet? Can you guys handle an extra 50/75 cars?<P>Just trying to keep a forum meet alive!||||reg||10
Z||000011||Rob S||07-27-2000||01:46 PM||||There is no such thing as too many Fieros, our show is open to ALL Fieros. The date for next years show has not been set, I think everyone in attendence liked the setup. The cars were displayed on a football sized field. There is plenty of room for more cars.<P>One draw back may be motel space in Onawa. Onawa is about 35 miles South of Sioux City on interstate 29, plenty of rooms there. <P>Rob Swanson<BR>Pierre SD<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||webbee||07-27-2000||09:03 PM||||What about it folks? Shall we all meet at this car show next year, days to be decided? Seems like it would work for the far north faction too, eh. Any body else think this would work?||||reg||5
